d_6294564e42239'),(58488,1795,'survey_index_7_survey_url_text','View Results'),(58489,1795,'_survey_index_7_survey_url_text','field_629456584223a'),(58490,1795,'survey_index','8'),(58491,1795,'_survey_index','field_6294561242236'),(58492,1795,'report_title','Download the report'),(58493,1795,'_report_title','field_62f30edfb57e1'),(58494,1795,'report_intro','Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Phasellus massa erat, consectetur at semper at, feugiat vel orci. '),(58495,1795,'_report_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(58496,1795,'report_link_url','#'),(58497,1795,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(58498,1795,'report_link_text','Download'),(58499,1795,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(58500,1795,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(58501,1795,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(58502,1795,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(58503,1795,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(58504,1795,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(58505,1795,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(58506,1795,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text