'_report_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(75568,1870,'report_link_url','#'),(75569,1870,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(75570,1870,'report_link_text','Download'),(75571,1870,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(75572,1870,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(75573,1870,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(75574,1870,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(75575,1870,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(75576,1870,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(75577,1870,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(75578,1870,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(75579,1870,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(75580,1870,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(75581,1870,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(75582,1870,'problem_icons','4'),(75583,1870,'_problem_icons','field_640fa0191d518'),(75584,1870,'ceh_content_left',''),(75585,1870,'_ceh_content_left','field_640e97e8f1c8c'),(75586,1870,'ceh_content_right',''),(75587,1870,'_ceh_content_right','field_640e97fdf1c8d'),(75588,1870