per at, feugiat vel orci. '),(76213,1871,'_report_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(76214,1871,'report_link_url','#'),(76215,1871,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(76216,1871,'report_link_text','Download'),(76217,1871,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(76218,1871,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(76219,1871,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(76220,1871,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(76221,1871,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(76222,1871,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(76223,1871,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(76224,1871,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(76225,1871,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(76226,1871,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(76227,1871,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(76228,1871,'problem_icons','4'),(76229,1871,'_problem_icons','field_640fa0191d518'),(76230,1871,'ceh_content_left',''),(76231,1871,'_ceh_content_left','field_640e97e8f1c8c'),(76232,1871,'ceh_content_right',''),(76233,1871,'_ceh_content_