561242236'),(83524,1917,'report_title','Download the report'),(83525,1917,'_report_title','field_62f30edfb57e1'),(83526,1917,'report_intro','Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Phasellus massa erat, consectetur at semper at, feugiat vel orci. '),(83527,1917,'_report_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(83528,1917,'report_link_url','#'),(83529,1917,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(83530,1917,'report_link_text','Download'),(83531,1917,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(83532,1917,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(83533,1917,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(83534,1917,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(83535,1917,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(83536,1917,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(83537,1917,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(83538,1917,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(83539,1917,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(83540,1917,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(83541,1917,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97')