Download'),(86225,1924,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(86226,1924,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(86227,1924,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(86228,1924,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(86229,1924,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(86230,1924,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(86231,1924,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(86232,1924,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(86233,1924,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(86234,1924,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(86235,1924,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(86236,1924,'problem_icons','4'),(86237,1924,'_problem_icons','field_640fa0191d518'),(86238,1924,'ceh_content_left',''),(86239,1924,'_ceh_content_left','field_640e97e8f1c8c'),(86240,1924,'ceh_content_right',''),(86241,1924,'_ceh_content_right','field_640e97fdf1c8d'),(86242,1924,'pc_content_left',''),(86243,1924,'_pc_content_left','field_640e983bf1c8f'),(86244,1924,'pc_content_right',''),(86245,1924,'_pc_content_right','field_640e984df