7e4'),(86904,1928,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(86905,1928,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(86906,1928,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(86907,1928,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(86908,1928,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(86909,1928,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(86910,1928,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(86911,1928,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(86912,1928,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(86913,1928,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(86914,1928,'problem_icons','4'),(86915,1928,'_problem_icons','field_640fa0191d518'),(86916,1928,'ceh_content_left',''),(86917,1928,'_ceh_content_left','field_640e97e8f1c8c'),(86918,1928,'ceh_content_right',''),(86919,1928,'_ceh_content_right','field_640e97fdf1c8d'),(86920,1928,'pc_content_left',''),(86921,1928,'_pc_content_left','field_640e983bf1c8f'),(86922,1928,'pc_content_right',''),(86923,1928,'_pc_content_right','field_640e984df1c90'),(86924,1928,'problem_icons_1_prob_icon','1699'),(8692