2,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(88932,1932,'report_link_text','Download'),(88933,1932,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(88934,1932,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(88935,1932,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(88936,1932,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(88937,1932,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(88938,1932,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(88939,1932,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(88940,1932,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(88941,1932,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(88942,1932,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(88943,1932,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(88944,1932,'problem_icons','4'),(88945,1932,'_problem_icons','field_640fa0191d518'),(88946,1932,'ceh_content_left',''),(88947,1932,'_ceh_content_left','field_640e97e8f1c8c'),(88948,1932,'ceh_content_right',''),(88949,1932,'_ceh_content_right','field_640e97fdf1c8d'),(88950,1932,'pc_content_left',''),(88951,1932,'_pc_content_left','field_640e983bf1c8f'),(88952,