57e4'),(112828,2070,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(112829,2070,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(112830,2070,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(112831,2070,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(112832,2070,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(112833,2070,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(112834,2070,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(112835,2070,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(112836,2070,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(112837,2070,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(112838,2070,'problem_icons','4'),(112839,2070,'_problem_icons','field_640fa0191d518'),(112840,2070,'ceh_content_left',''),(112841,2070,'_ceh_content_left','field_640e97e8f1c8c'),(112842,2070,'ceh_content_right',''),(112843,2070,'_ceh_content_right','field_640e97fdf1c8d'),(112844,2070,'pc_content_left',''),(112845,2070,'_pc_content_left','field_640e983bf1c8f'),(112846,2070,'pc_content_right',''),(112847,2070,'_pc_content_right','field_640e984df1c90'),(112848,2070,'problem_icons_1_pr