ro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(122401,2163,'report_link_url','#'),(122402,2163,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(122403,2163,'report_link_text','Download'),(122404,2163,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(122405,2163,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(122406,2163,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(122407,2163,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(122408,2163,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(122409,2163,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(122410,2163,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(122411,2163,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(122412,2163,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(122413,2163,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(122414,2163,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(122415,2163,'problem_icons','4'),(122416,2163,'_problem_icons','field_640fa0191d518'),(122417,2163,'ceh_content_left',''),(122418,2163,'_ceh_content_left','field_640e97e8f1c8c'),(122419,2163,'ceh_content_right',''),(122420,2163,'_ceh_content_right','field_640e97fdf1c8d'),(12