t_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(154226,2458,'report_link_url','#'),(154227,2458,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(154228,2458,'report_link_text','Download'),(154229,2458,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(154230,2458,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(154231,2458,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(154232,2458,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(154233,2458,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(154234,2458,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(154235,2458,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(154236,2458,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(154237,2458,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(154238,2458,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(154239,2458,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(154240,2458,'problem_icons','4'),(154241,2458,'_problem_icons','field_640fa0191d518'),(154242,2458,'ceh_content_left',''),(154243,2458,'_ceh_content_left','field_640e97e8f1c8c'),(154244,2458,'ceh_content_right',''),(154245,2458,'_ceh_content_right','field_640e97fdf1c8d'