url_text','View Results'),(154949,2459,'_survey_index_7_survey_url_text','field_629456584223a'),(154950,2459,'survey_index','8'),(154951,2459,'_survey_index','field_6294561242236'),(154952,2459,'report_title','Download the report'),(154953,2459,'_report_title','field_62f30edfb57e1'),(154954,2459,'report_intro','Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Phasellus massa erat, consectetur at semper at, feugiat vel orci. '),(154955,2459,'_report_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(154956,2459,'report_link_url','#'),(154957,2459,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(154958,2459,'report_link_text','Download'),(154959,2459,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(154960,2459,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(154961,2459,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(154962,2459,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(154963,2459,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(154964,2459,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(154965,2459,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(154966,2459,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(154967,2