nable pathways for people to find a place to call home.</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->','Home','','inherit','closed','closed','','6-revision-v1','','','2023-09-10 23:53:48','2023-09-10 23:53:48','',6,'http://localhost/?p=1875',0,'revision','',0),(1876,1,'2023-09-10 23:54:26','2023-09-10 23:54:26','<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Everybody’s home is different, but we all want the same thing: a place to build a fulfilling life.</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Australia is a rich country, but despite our growing national wealth, for many people the Australian dream seems increasingly out of reach.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Renters are seeing huge price increases and insecure tenancy agreements.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>First home buyers are struggling to scrape together a deposit.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Low-income families are facing years on the waiting list for social housing.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Housing policies at the national, state, and local level are failing to provide reasonable pathways for people to find a place to call home.</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->','Home','','inherit','closed','closed','','6-revision-v1','','','2023-09-10 23:54:26','2023-09-10 23:54:26','',6,'http://localhost/?p=1876',0,'revision','',0),(1878,1,'2023-09-21 08:09:20','2023-09-21 08:09:20','<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Queenslanders want more protected areas to safeguard our native plants and animals, our cultural history and our way of life in the great outdoors. Here\'s what that looks like...</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"32px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:32px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"32px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:32px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" id=\"parks\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaPosition\":\"right\",\"mediaId\":166,\"mediaLink\":\"https://protectqueensland.org.au/2021/09/conservationists-welcome-handback-of-world-heritage-listed-national-parks-to-daintree-traditional-owners/img_8090/\",\"mediaType\":\"image\",\"imageFill\":true,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.18,\"y\":0.51}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile is-image-fill\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Partnerships with First Nations People</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>There is now global acknowledgement that a focus on nature conservation should never be at the exclusion of living Indigenous cultures.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Queensland’s Landmark Cape York Tenure Resolution Program delivers a leading consent-based model of negotiating new Aboriginal owned national parks.&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This world-leading model has been extended to the World Heritage-listed Daintree, Minjerribah and Boodjamulla (Lawn Hill) National Parks.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Joint management creates employment opportunities and increases in revenue streams, as well as significant socio-economic benefits for regional and remote communities.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"textColor\":\"black\",\"className\":\"btn btn-block\"} -->\n<p class=\"btn btn-block has-black-color has-text-color\"><strong><a href=\"https://protectqueensland.org.au/campaigns/cape-york-peninsula/\" title=\"Cape York\">Find out more</a></strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\" style=\"background-image:url(https://protectqueensland.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/IMG_8090-1024x768.jpg);background-position:18% 51%\"><img src=\"https://protectqueensland.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/IMG_8090-1024x768.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-166 size-full\"/></figure></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaId\":388,\"mediaLink\":\"https://protectqueensland.org.au/big-crystal-creek/\",\"mediaType\":\"image\",\"imageFill\":true,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.57,\"y\":0.64}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile is-image-fill\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\" style=\"background-image:url(https://protectqueensland.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/RS5424_141757-19-lpr-682x1024.jpg);background-position:57% 64%\"><img src=\"https://protectqueensland.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/RS5424_141757-19-lpr-682x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-388 size-full\"/></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">More Queensland National Parks</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>As Queenslanders, we are lucky to live in one of the most wildlife-rich places on the planet.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>National parks provide a legal safeguard for this wildlife.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Our parks are home to many endangered species of plants and animals, many of which would face uncertain futures without the protection of their park habitat.&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>And it’s not just Queensland’s wildlife that benefit from our parks.&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Our protected areas provide places for exploration and exercise, rest and recuperation. They are the place where generations of families have made incredible memories together – walking, swimming, sleeping under the stars.&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Our parks also provide a clear, tangible connection to one of the oldest cultures on Earth. First Nations Australians have been here for more than 50,000 years, and parks provide legal protection for the landscapes they have been connected with for thousands of generations.&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"btn btn-block\"} -->\n<p class=\"btn btn-block\"><strong><a href=\"https://protectqueensland.org.au/campaigns/more-national-parks/\" title=\"Our National Parks\">Find out more</a></strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"55px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:55px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" id=\"forests\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaPosition\":\"right\",\"mediaId\":373,\"mediaLink\":\"https://protectqueensland.org.au/picture1/\",\"mediaType\":\"image\",\"imageFill\":true,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.56,\"y\":0.34}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile is-image-fill\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Protecting Native Forests</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Native State Forests in Queensland are more than just trees - they represent a vast and irreplaceable ecological treasure. These forests provide a critical habitat for threatened and endangered species and act as significant carbon stores, making their protection crucial for Queensland and Australia\'s environmental credibility.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Transitioning these State Forests to conservation reserves would not only benefit nature but also regional communities. National and conservation parks generate billions in annual revenue from tourism, providing employment and recreational opportunities for locals and visitors in hospitality and nature-based tourism.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"btn btn-block\"} -->\n<p class=\"btn btn-block\"><strong><a href=\"https://protectqueensland.org.au/campaigns/protect-native-forests/\" title=\"Protect Native Forests\">Find out more</a></strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\" style=\"background-image:url(https://protectqueensland.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Picture1-683x1024.jpg);background-position:56% 34%\"><img src=\"https://protectqueensland.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Picture1-683x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-373 size-full\"/></figure></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"55px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:55px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" id=\"refuges\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaId\":270,\"mediaLink\":\"https://protectqueensland.org.au/how/dcim103goprog0055512-jpg/\",\"mediaType\":\"image\",\"imageFill\":true,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.55,\"y\":0.52}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile is-image-fill\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\" style=\"background-image:url(https://protectqueensland.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/RS4361_G0055512-lpr-background-1024x456.jpg);background-position:55% 52%\"><img src=\"https://protectqueensland.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/RS4361_G0055512-lpr-background-1024x456.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-270 size-full\"/></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">More private protected areas</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Private protected areas are also an important part of the solution. Queensland is home to the nation’s largest private protected area program, called the Nature Refuges program.&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This program allows landholders to access funding to undertake conservation work on their properties, while placing permanent protections on parts of their land.&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Unfortunately, this vital program is now dangerously underfunded</strong>, meaning landholders wishing to access it are not being given the chance.&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"btn btn-block\"} -->\n<p class=\"btn btn-block\"><strong><a href=\"/campaigns/nature-refuges/\" title=\"\">Find out more</a></strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer -->\n<div style=\"height:100px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->','How','','publish','closed','closed','','how','','','2023-09-21 08:22:36','2023-09-21 08:22:36','',0,'http://localhost/?page_id=1878',0,'page','',0),(1879,1,'2023-09-21 08:09:20','2023-09-21 08:09:20','<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Queenslanders want more protected areas to safeguard our native plants and animals, our cultural history and our way of life in the great outdoors. Here\'s what that looks like...</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"55px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:55px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"55px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:55px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" id=\"parks\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"55px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:55px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" id=\"partnership\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaPosition\":\"right\",\"mediaId\":166,\"mediaLink\":\"https://protectqueensland.org.au/2021/09/conservationists-welcome-handback-of-world-heritage-listed-national-parks-to-daintree-traditional-owners/im